WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:45.625


2
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:48.000
<b>This chapter of the Gita is called</b>

3
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.333
<b>Arjuna Vishada Yoga. </b>

4
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:52.833
<b>Arjuna's mind is being torn apart.</b>

5
00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:54.583
<b>He cannot understand</b>

6
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:59.416
<b>how he can be happy by killing his</b>
<b>own people in this way.</b>

7
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:04.208


8
00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:05.916
<b>Inside Arjuna's mind,</b>

9
00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:10.916
<b>the stream of conflicts, arguments,</b>
<b>and counter-arguments is not stopping at all.</b>

10
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:11.791
<b>Arjuna, </b>

11
00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:13.875
<b>if you forgive them,</b>

12
00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:16.500
<b>will they also abandon this war?</b>

13
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.250
<b>Will they not kill anyone?</b>

14
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.541
<b>And why would they do that?</b>

15
00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:25.000
<b>These people have forgotten dharma</b>
<b>in their desire for kingdom and power, Krishna.</b>

16
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.541
<b>They have become blind.</b>

17
00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:29.875
<b>They cannot even see</b>
<b>the grave sin inherent in all this.</b>

18
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:32.333
<b>They do not see anyone</b>
<b>as their own or as others.</b>

19
00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:35.666
<b>They will kill anyone to win the war.</b>

20
00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:38.666
<b> You have also been challenged for war.</b>

21
00:01:38.666 --> 00:01:40.833
<b>You will also be attacked.</b>

22
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.291
<b>Will you bow your head?</b>

23
00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:45.833
<b>Will you abandon the Kshatriya dharma</b>
<b>in such a situation?</b>

24
00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:46.791
<b>Dharma, </b>

25
00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:49.916
<b>The purpose of dharma</b>
<b>is human welfare, isn't it? </b>

26
00:01:49.916 --> 00:01:51.208
<b>It is for the good, isn't it?</b>

27
00:01:51.208 --> 00:01:56.125
<b>What kind of dharma is this in which</b>
<b>I also kill my own people like them?</b>

28
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:57.875
<b>They are immersed in desire,</b>

29
00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:59.208
<b>but I am not.</b>

30
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:04.666
<b>I cannot abandon my goodness</b>
<b>because of their vile nature.</b>

31
00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:05.750
<b>It will end,</b>

32
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.291
<b>there will be an end,</b>

33
00:02:07.291 --> 00:02:10.666
<b>there will be an end to this sorrow as well.</b>

34
00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:19.416
<b>The light of Lord Krishna's teachings will surely</b>
<b>destroy the darkness that surrounds Arjuna.</b>

35
00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:24.250


36
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:29.791
<b>Just as nectar emerged after the</b>
<b>terrible churning of the ocean,</b>

37
00:02:29.791 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>the decision that will emerge after</b>
<b>Arjuna's self-churning</b>

38
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>will be powerful </b>

39
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:37.125
<b>and unshakable.</b>

40
00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:39.291
<b>And this self-churning</b>

41
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:43.458
<b>should not be considered</b>
<b>a symbol of weakness at all.</b>

42
00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:49.291
<b>Arjuna is fully capable of victory in war,</b>

43
00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:51.250
<b>but</b>

44
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:56.916
<b>he does not want this victory by</b>
<b>putting his morality at stake.</b>

45
00:02:56.916 --> 00:03:01.333
<b>This is the light of Arjuna's values, </b>

46
00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:06.083
<b>the mark of his morality.</b>

47
00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:09.291
<b>If Duryodhana were in his place,</b>

48
00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:11.708
<b>he would forget all sin and virtue</b>

49
00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:15.000
<b>and do every deception,</b>
<b>every deceit, </b>

50
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.958
<b>just to secure victory in his fist.</b>

51
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:20.708
<b>And for this very reason,</b>

52
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:25.125
<b>he will never achieve this victory.</b>

53
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:32.125
<b>Victory earned through misconduct</b>
<b>and illegitimate acts is like a fake diamond.</b>

54
00:03:32.125 --> 00:03:35.666
<b>The shine and glitter it possesses</b>

55
00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:38.333
<b>quickly begin to fade.</b>

56
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:42.750
<b>This fake diamond shatters under</b>
<b>the pressure of time.</b>

57
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.958
<b>And there,</b>

58
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.125
<b>your values,</b>

59
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.833
<b>your conscience,</b>

60
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:49.916
<b>also lend your victory</b>

61
00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:54.791
<b>the shine of a true diamond, </b>

62
00:03:54.791 --> 00:03:56.916
<b>and strength too.</b>

63
00:03:56.916 --> 00:04:00.125
<b>This victory neither ever fades</b>

64
00:04:00.125 --> 00:04:03.583
<b>nor disintegrates under the pressure of time.</b>

65
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:08.666
<b>Never forget moral values in your personal life.</b>

66
00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:14.291


67
00:04:14.291 --> 00:04:16.750
<b>Yes,</b>

68
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.375
<b>Arjuna is certainly entangled,</b>

69
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:22.625
<b>but he will also resolve his dilemma.</b>

70
00:04:22.625 --> 00:04:23.916
<b>However,</b>

71
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:25.916
<b>his thoughts</b>

72
00:04:25.916 --> 00:04:27.791
<b>are not that</b>

73
00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:30.166
<b>if his Pandava brothers fight,</b>

74
00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:32.458
<b>he should also fight,</b>

75
00:04:32.458 --> 00:04:35.541
<b>nor are his thoughts that if </b>

76
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.916
<b>his enemies display strength, </b>

77
00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:41.708
<b>he should do the same.</b>

78
00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:43.666
<b>His thinking</b>

79
00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:47.166
<b>is completely independent of others.</b>

80
00:04:47.166 --> 00:04:49.375
<b>In social life,</b>

81
00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:50.833
<b>we</b>

82
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:56.666
<b>lose this freedom countless times</b>
<b>without realizing it. </b>

83
00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:58.375
<b>Without knowing,</b>

84
00:04:58.375 --> 00:05:01.875
<b>we start following someone else. </b>

85
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:03.625
<b>Someone else's attire,</b>

86
00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:04.708
<b>lifestyle,</b>

87
00:05:04.708 --> 00:05:05.791
<b>glitz and glamour,</b>

88
00:05:05.791 --> 00:05:08.458
<b>some expensive ornament.</b>

89
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:14.375
<b>We also become eager to attain all that,</b>

90
00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:15.291
<b>so that</b>

91
00:05:15.291 --> 00:05:18.625
<b>we can match that person.</b>

92
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:20.375
<b>Under social pressure,</b>

93
00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:23.791
<b>in the aspiration to be part of a group,</b>

94
00:05:23.791 --> 00:05:28.041
<b>we become, what we are not.</b>

95
00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:30.625
<b>Take inspiration from others,</b>

96
00:05:30.625 --> 00:05:31.541
<b>learn,</b>

97
00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:32.416
<b> observe, </b>

98
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:34.083
<b>but</b>

99
00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:39.208
<b>keep your thoughts and</b>
<b>personality independent.</b>

100
00:05:39.208 --> 00:05:46.916
<b>In this world, there are no</b>
<b>two individuals with the same fingerprints.</b>

101
00:05:46.916 --> 00:05:49.416
<b>There must be a reason.</b>

102
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:52.041
<b>Every person is unique,</b>

103
00:05:52.041 --> 00:05:54.125
<b>special.</b>

104
00:05:54.125 --> 00:06:02.125
<b>What is the need for you to become</b>
<b>like someone else under social pressure?</b>

105
00:06:02.125 --> 00:06:05.000
<b>Recognize your uniqueness.</b>

106
00:06:05.458 --> 00:06:09.625


107
00:06:09.625 --> 00:06:16.125
<b>Arjuna's principles give us a great lesson</b>
<b>for professional life.</b>

108
00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:17.583
<b>In business,</b>

109
00:06:17.583 --> 00:06:18.958
<b>in employment,</b>

110
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:20.500
<b>your morality</b>

111
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.000
<b>and your ideals</b>

112
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.250
<b>are like the two front lights of a vehicle.</b>

113
00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.958
<b>In the light of day,</b>

114
00:06:27.958 --> 00:06:31.416
<b>anyone can travel without them.</b>

115
00:06:31.416 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>However,</b>

116
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.791
<b>as soon as darkness falls, </b>

117
00:06:34.791 --> 00:06:37.708
<b> such a journey will come to a halt.</b>

118
00:06:37.708 --> 00:06:39.791
<b>On the other hand,</b>

119
00:06:39.791 --> 00:06:44.291
<b>whoever proceeds with these</b>
<b>two lights illuminated</b>

120
00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:46.666
<b>will have no fear of darkness,</b>

121
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:48.125
<b>and that </b>

122
00:06:48.125 --> 00:06:51.875
<b>person will be able to cover a long distance.</b>

123
00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:54.500
<b>One whose foundation is morality,</b>

124
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.125
<b>their victory will endure.</b>

125
00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.375
<b>Think about it.</b>

